      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (2. seconds per picture)</b> - How many seconds each picture stays on screen.</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (3. frames per second)</b> - Frames per second of the video. 30 is smooth and common; 24 looks like film. The same number goes to the Math node and to Save Mp4.</li><li><b>Resize Crop Pixaroma (4. video size)</b> - Makes every picture the video size, here a <b>1080 x 1080</b> square, by cropping the edges. A video needs every frame to be the same size.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Math Expression (frames per picture = a x b)</b> - Works out how many frames each picture needs: <code>a * b</code> = seconds per picture x frames per second. 2 x 30 = 60 frames.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Repeat Image Batch (holds each picture)</b> - Repeats each picture that many times, so it holds still on screen for the seconds you set.</li><li><b>Rebatch Images (all frames into one video)</b> - Joins the frames of every picture into ONE long batch, so the video gets them all at once instead of making one tiny video per picture.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Mp4 Pixaroma (the slideshow)</b> - Turns the frames into an MP4 video and plays it right on the node. It is saved into <code>ComfyUI/output/Slideshow</code>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (2. seconds per picture)</b> - How many seconds each picture stays on screen.</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (3. frames per second)</b> - Frames per second of the video. 30 is smooth and common; 24 looks like film. The same number goes to the Math node and to Save Mp4.</li><li><b>Resize Crop Pixaroma (4. video size)</b> - Makes every picture the video size, here a <b>1080 x 1080</b> square, by cropping the edges. A video needs every frame to be the same size.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Math Expression (frames per picture = a x b)</b> - Works out how many frames each picture needs: <code>a * b</code> = seconds per picture x frames per second. 2 x 30 = 60 frames.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\